-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       R-Type
  Publisher   Electric Dreams, 1988
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        r_type.z80
  MD5         5a2179b4006d7888a1f7f821a4316bf5

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.0: first NXC patch, from the nexclash r_type SpecNext build
              with the loading screen at ENTER

  Note        Layer 2 scenery with half-pixel hardware scroll, figures as
              filled hardware sprites that glide, four pictures per game
              update; the original code runs as the logic. Start-up shows a
              technical-spec screen (Advanced intro screen toggle). The game
              file is the 128K snapshot (a tape cannot be the target: level
              data is converted at load). The loading screen shows from ENTER
              and needs the current NXC loader (NEXCLASH). Too large for the
              in-NEX menu: the loader builds it with your choices. Needs a 2MB
              Next. Not verified: a full playthrough; the replay check was not
              run (no recordings).

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Absolute invincibility
   4  Immortality

